    {
      "name": "Marsh Causeway",
      "note": "North\u2013south over the tidal estuary, from the head of the inlet down to the Seaview shore. Its north end used to be drawn eight tiles out in open water, so the deck had land on one side only and the no-piers pass reverted the whole causeway to sea; it now starts on the bank at the head of the inlet. It crosses the estuary at its widest, and 96 tiles of water on this line is what sets maxBridgeSpan: 90 is not enough, 96 is. The narrowest point of the same strait is 22 tiles, 33 tiles west at x=532 \u2014 moving the causeway there would make it an ordinary bridge, but it would no longer join Market Square to the Seaview shore, which is the connection it was drawn for.",
